title: Payers › Test Workflow › Fix in builder
route: /payers/summit?tab=test
intro: When a test stops where it should not, 'Fix in builder' opens the builder on that workflow with the step it stopped at already selected, so the fix is a few clicks away.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "A test run has finished\nResults show 'Fix in builder' and a line: 'Opens the builder at the step where it stopped.'"
decision d1 "Did it stop at a step?"
click c1 "Click 'Fix in builder'"
process p1 "The address becomes ?tab=builder&workflow=the-id&node=the-step"
screen b1 "Workflow Builder opens on that workflow\nThe stopping step is selected, the canvas moves to it and its settings are open"
screen b2 "No step is named: the builder opens on the workflow, nothing selected\n'Opens the builder on this workflow.'"
click c2 "Change the step: its condition, documents, rule or the line after it"
process p2 "Edits are held in the builder until 'Save draft'"
decision d2 "Is the workflow published?"
store st1 "'Save draft' makes a draft of the next version\nThe published one keeps serving cases"
store st2 "'Save draft' saves the draft in place"
click c3 "Click 'Test'"
process p3 "Saves the draft, then returns to Test Workflow with the same workflow\nThe made-up case is the one chosen again"
screen t1 "Run it again: the result is labelled 'Draft: not used for cases yet'\nuntil the draft is published"
end e1 "The fix is tested before anyone publishes it"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Save a draft and publish"

s1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| c1 --> p1 --> b1 --> c2 --> p2 --> d2
d1 -->|No| c1
p1 --> b2
d2 -->|Yes| st1 --> c3
d2 -->|No| st2 --> c3
c3 --> p3 --> t1 --> e1 --> g1
